- ## Solved transformation
Input is an n×n grid; output is 2n×2n, formed from four orientations of the input in the quadrants:

- top-left: input unchanged `A`;
- top-right: input rotated 180° (`rot180(A)`);
- bottom-left: input transposed (`Aᵀ`). This is explicitly confirmed by demo 3, whose input is asymmetric.
- bottom-right: input horizontally mirrored (each row reversed; left-right reflection of `A`).
